From bb45a9a60291376677fed9cb3d32f3e06c06a4d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 13:07:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1 3/4] media: qcom: camss: vfe-gen2: never arm the write
 master with a zero pong buffer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A clean capture on the Galaxy A52 (sc7180, vfe-170) still faulted the IFE
SMMU context bank on stream-on:

  arm-smmu 15000000.iommu: Unhandled context fault: fsr=0x402,
      iova=0x00000000, fsynr=0x1c0011, cbfrsynra=0x820, cb=8
  FSR = [Format=2 TF], FSYNR0 = [WNR PLVL=1]

cbfrsynra 0x820 is the VFE0 SID, WNR is a write: the VFE write master
DMAed a frame to IOVA 0. Once the fault is taken the context bank wedges
and all further camss capture fails until reboot, so the camera hangs
with no frames.

The gen2 write master double-buffers its image address into an internal
ping/pong pair and consumes one slot per frame. vfe_enable_output_v2()
programs one slot per queued buffer, up to CAMSS_INIT_BUF_COUNT (2). With
min_queued_buffers = 1, vb2 may start streaming with a single buffer
queued, so only the ping slot gets an address and the pong slot keeps its
reset value of 0 - the hardware then writes one frame to IOVA 0.

The existing guard only handled the zero-buffer case. Handle the
single-buffer case the same way the gen1 path already does in
vfe_output_init_addrs() (pong_addr = ping_addr): point the spare slot at
the same buffer so the write master never targets address 0. A second
buffer queued later via vfe_queue_buffer_v2() reprograms the slot.

Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
index 295f9df412e5..43d10970b709 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
@@ -570,6 +570,22 @@ int vfe_enable_output_v2(struct vfe_line *line)
 		return -ENOBUFS;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The write master double-buffers its image address into an internal
+	 * ping/pong pair and consumes one slot per frame. The loop above
+	 * programs one slot per queued buffer, so if only a single buffer was
+	 * available the second slot is left at its reset value of 0. The
+	 * hardware would then DMA a frame to IOVA 0, fault the IFE SMMU context
+	 * bank (TF, WNR) and wedge all further capture. Point the spare slot at
+	 * the same buffer so the master never targets address 0, mirroring the
+	 * gen1 path (vfe_output_init_addrs(): pong_addr = ping_addr).
+	 */
+	if (output->gen2.active_num == 1) {
+		ops->vfe_wm_update(vfe, output->wm_idx[0],
+				   output->buf[0]->addr[0], line);
+		ops->reg_update(vfe, line->id);
+	}
+
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&vfe->output_lock, flags);
 
 	return 0;
